      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2011 Blackwell Publishing Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "Human leucocyte antigen-G (HLA-G) is a non-classical HLA class I molecule demonstrated originally in placental trophoblast cells. Recognition of the importance of HLA-G to the maternal immune accommodation of the semi-allogeneic fetus has led to investigations of its role in the suppression of immune responses and induction of tolerance. More recently, HLA-G has been shown to have increased expression in several immunological diseases including asthma and allergic rhinitis. The focus of this review is the potential role of HLA-G in immunological airway diseases."
      },
